Spar's SCIM token and SCIM external-id stores can now be migrated from Cassandra to PostgreSQL. To migrate an existing installation: set `spar.config.postgresMigration.scimTokens` and `spar.config.postgresMigration.scimExternalIds` to `migration-to-postgresql` (dual writes), then enable `background-worker.config.migrateScimTokens` and `background-worker.config.migrateScimExternalIds` and wait for the `wire_scim_tokens_migration_finished` and `wire_scim_external_ids_migration_finished` metrics to reach `1.0`, then switch both settings to `postgresql` and disable the two migration flags. See the "Using PostgreSQL for storing Cassandra-backed data" section of the configuration docs for details.
